  "answer": "The emails regarding Project Zenith cover the following timeline and details:\n\n1. **Initiation (July 2023)**: The project was announced to start in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff meeting on July 15th. The goal is to optimize cloud storage solutions for security and accessibility. A call for ideas was issued by July 20th, focusing on leveraging AI for data visualization.\n2. **Team Expansion**: The team was expanded to accelerate progress. Initially, five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture were added, with an onboarding session on September 10th. Later, Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing) were welcomed.\n3. **Development and Design**: Following the design phase, the project moved to the development phase starting the following month, with Omar Jensen as the lead developer providing guidance.\n4. **Training**: HR Manager Jane Doe approved a $15,000 budget for specialized training for the coding team and project managers, scheduled to start the following month.\n5. **Findings and Milestones**: Initial findings suggested a potential 20% efficiency increase using proposed AI algorithms, to be discussed in a meeting on August 5th. A significant milestone was reached with the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th.\n6. **Feedback**: Feedback was sought from stakeholders regarding the prototype's performance and user experience, with a submission deadline at the end of November."
